The c-binding documentation is severely lacking for the more complex reflections, especially QList. I was trying to add custom headers to my pdf object but couldn't find any help, neither in the documentation, nor in the issues, nor on Google.

The only issue I could find about the subject was #3065, which had garnered no response. I don't know whether the knowledge of how the QList reflection works was lost or not, but I hope I can explain it here to help other people and perhaps get someone to complete the documentation. The following is based on version 0.12.4

# QList reflection

Unlike simpler structures, QLists require multiple calls to wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting to work. QList reflection allows us to manipulate the QList with 4 functions:

- clear (clears all elements in the list)
- append (adds an element at the end of the list) 
- prepend (adds an element in front of the list)
- delete (deletes the nth element, n is provided by the value parameter)

The QList starts empty, so we must add elements to it before setting their value. Elements can be set with the following syntax :

- [n] (where n is the zero-based index of the element)
- first (equivalent to [0])
- last (targets the last element in the list)

To call these functions or set the elements we must append the descriptor to the name of the property we want to change, separated by a dot.
The value will only be used by setters and the delete function, other functions ignore it. For setters, the value is passed to the appropriate reflector for the property you're setting.

# Example

Below is a full example of how to use the reflection to set the load.customHeaders setting:

```c++
// create an object setting object
wkhtmltopdf_object_settings *os = wkhtmltopdf_create_object_settings();

// clear the list for demonstration purposes
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.clear", "");

// add a few custom header slots
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.append", "");
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.append", "");
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.prepend", "");
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.prepend", "");

// set their value
// note: load.customHeaders is a QList<QPair<QString, QString>>
//         QPair<QString, QString> expects the two string seperated by a '\n'
//
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.first", "Host\nmyserver.com");
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.[1]", "Test-Header\nTest");
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.[2]", "Hello\nWorld");
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.last", "Useless-Header\nUseless value");

// delete the 4th header because we don't actually want it
// remember the list's index is zero_based
wkhtmltopdf_set_object_setting(os, "load.customHeaders.delete", "3");

/* do stuff with the object setting */
```

